# ==================================================================================================
# .gitattributes - This states how Git stores each kind of file 
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This project was edited on windows but was build and run in Linux containers. So these rules make
# every checkout identical on both platforms. This is important for reproducible builds and also to
# track back to the exact files of the tagged comit that produced it.
# ==================================================================================================

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test files: always LF line endings
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Git decides which files are text, stores them with LF, and also checks them out with LF on Windows.
# Without this, Git reports "changes" in files nobody edited, and a Windows line ending (CRLF) can 
# break the Linux side.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts run inside the Linux container (for example the container entrypoint 
# docker/entrypoint.sh). A CRLF ending makes bash fail to start them, so they are always text with
# LF, never left to Git's guess.
*.sh text eol=lf

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Robot Meshes (copied directly from original v1.0 release)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# binary            : store the file exactly as it is: no line-ending changes, no line-by-line
#                     diff or merge. This already went wrong once: six .dae files were converted
#                     to CRLF on Windows and had to be restored before they matched v1.0.0.
# linguist-vendored : third-party files; GitHub leaves them out of the "languages used" bar.
*.dae binary linguist-vendored
*.stl binary linguist-vendored
src/iiwa_sim/meshes/** linguist-vendored

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Images (Resulting graphs are in Docs) {Stored in yte for byte, to avoid line-ending conversion}
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.jpg binary
